spans.s:
सिद्ध a. hit (aim), attained;
 brought about, accomplished,
prepared, ready;
 settled, established, known, valid;
 resulting,
following;
 fallen to one's share, one's own;
 peculiar, particular;
perfected^1 or sanctified;
 thoroughly skilled in magical arts or endowed
with supernatural powers. m. seer, fortune-teller, a great saint or one
of the blessed (a class of semi-divine beings). n. supernatural power,
magic art.
[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.

सिद्धार्थ a. = prec. or leading to the goal,
effective, powerful;
 m. E. of Buddha.

सिद्धि f. hitting or reaching the aim, attainment of an
object, performance, accomplishment, conclusion, result;
 success,
prosperity, welfare;
 perfection, supernatural power.
